# There is nothing to configure for the app itself.
#
# Sync needs no account, no API keys and no third-party service. It uses a
# serverless function on your own Vercel project (api/sync.js) plus a
# Vercel Blob store, and the data in it is encrypted on your device before
# it is sent — the server holds ciphertext it cannot read.
#
# The one variable it needs, BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN, is injected
# automatically by Vercel when you connect a Blob store to the project:
#
#   Vercel dashboard → Storage → Create Database → Blob
#     → Connect to this project → Redeploy
#
# You only need the line below for running the function locally with
# `vercel dev`. Copy the token from Vercel → Storage → your store → .env.local
#
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=vercel_blob_rw_xxxxxxxx
